nfidence": 0.94, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "The window [4765,43165] contains 5150 events over 1901 active nodes (step_01), but source node 1330 participates in none of them: zero events, zero distinct partners (step_02), zero neighbours in either direction (step_03), and its 2-hop neighbourhood collapses to the single isolated node itself (step_07). A partition of the timeline confirms all 7 of 1330's lifetime events (step_04) occur strictly after the window ends, from 43166 onward (step_06, step_12). With no first hop available, no time-respecting path with <=600-unit gaps can leave 1330 inside the window, so the cascade is absent rather than merely unobserved. Three confounders were tested and rejected as explanations. (1) Static reachability: ignoring time, 1330 does connect to the wider graph via 399, 669, 678, 681 and 724, and hub 28 bridges toward 361 (step_09) - but this aggregate path is a time-ignoring artefact. (2) Hub popularity: node 28 is extremely active in the window (383 events, 299 partners) and even contacts 361 directly once (step_10, step_11), which would make a naive volume- or popularity-based test fire; however that traffic cannot be seeded by 1330, which is silent. (3) Target liveness: 361 is genuinely active in the window with 4 events spread across it (step_02, step_13) and 5 more afterwards (step_14), so the negative result is not caused by a dead target - it is caused specifically by the source's activity lying entirely outside and after the interval."}, "raw_final_response": "All evidence converges: **node 1330 has zero events in [4765, 43165]**, so no cascade can originate from it there.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_dc3dfaa5\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1330, 361],\n  \"window\": [4765, 43165],\n  \"confidence\": 0.94,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The window [4765,43165] contains 5150 events over 1901 active nodes (step_01), but source node 1330 participates in none of them: zero events, zero distinct partners (step_02), zero neighbours in either direction (step_03), and its 2-hop neighbourhood collapses to the single isolated node itself (step_07). A partition of the timeline confirms all 7 of 1330's lifetime events (step_04) occur strictly after the window ends, from 43166 onward (step_06, step_12). With no first hop available, no time-respecting path with <=600-unit gaps can leave 1330 inside the window, so the cascade is absent rather than merely unobserved. Three confounders were tested and rejected as explanations. (1) Static reachability: ignoring time, 1330 does connect to the wider graph via 399, 669, 678, 681 and 724, and hub 28 bridges toward 361 (step_09) - but this aggregate path is a time-ignoring artefact. (2) Hub popularity: node 28 is extremely active in the window (383 events, 299 partners) and even contacts 361 directly once (step_10, step_11), which would make a naive volume- or popularity-based test fire; however that traffic cannot be seeded by 1330, which is silent. (3) Target liveness: 361 is genuinely active in the window with 4 events spread across it (step_02, step_13) and 5 more afterwards (step_14), so the negative result is not caused by a dead target - it is caused specifically by the source's activity lying entirely outside and after the interval.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 42830, "total_output_tokens": 3499, "total_tokens": 46329, "total_latency_ms": 66455, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}